From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Finn Freas <finn.freas@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xilinx: read pblocks from the XDC

create_pblock, add_cells_to_pblock and resize_pblock -add build a
placement Region per pblock, as Vivado's XDC describes one:

- add_cells_to_pblock takes the get_cells forms the parser already
  reads; a name that is no leaf cell is taken as a hierarchical
  instance, so [get_cells u_rm] takes every flattened cell named
  "u_rm.*" (or "u_rm/..." in Vivado's separator), and every cell whose
  scopename attribute (yosys flatten -scopename) lies under u_rm.
- resize_pblock -add takes site ranges such as
  SLICE_X12Y100:SLICE_X15Y149, matched by site type and site
  coordinates rather than the tile grid, so a SLICE range takes no
  block RAM or DSP site.
- set_property EXCLUDE_PLACEMENT true [get_pblocks <name>] makes the
  pblock exclusive: isBelLocationValid then keeps every cell that is
  not a member off its bels.  Other pblock properties are ignored
  with a warning.

The XDC is read before packing, so after pack_lutffs the pblocks are
carried to what packing made: a cell named after the netlist cell it
was made from takes that cell's pblock, and every cell of a cluster
takes the pblock of its members, so that the root carries it to the
placer.  A member without a bel of its type in its pblock is an error.
The block RAM regrowth after placement now honours a cell's region.

The router is not constrained: a Region bounds bels only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
